{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/431545-unsettling-gaze","id":431545,"title":"Unsettling Gaze","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-07T11:30:59-08:00","id":431545,"title":"Unsettling Gaze","content":"How do we feel about this merit, you guys? I like the idea of it a lot, but it feels like it could be simpler/easier to use. As it is, it predicates on both the opponent having higher Humanity AND the exceptional success, which seems useful for an older Nosferatu, but not very useful at all for those with low Blood Potency. Then there's the drawback, which I don't really have a beef with.<br /> <br /> Is there any way we could simplify it? What if, instead of requiring the exceptional success, it requires a regular success + 1 WP?<br /> <br /> And lastly, a question for clarification: What penalty/level of sin should Unsettling Gaze trigger for Integrity/Humanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-07-2015, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:13:51-08:00","id":431613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/431545-unsettling-gaze#post431545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do we feel about this merit, you guys? I like the idea of it a lot, but it feels like it could be simpler/easier to use. As it is, it predicates on both the opponent having higher Humanity AND the exceptional success, which seems useful for an older Nosferatu, but not very useful at all for those with low Blood Potency. Then there's the drawback, which I don't really have a beef with.<br /> <br /> Is there any way we could simplify it? What if, instead of requiring the exceptional success, it requires a regular success + 1 WP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems reasonable to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/431545-unsettling-gaze#post431545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And lastly, a question for clarification: What penalty/level of sin should Unsettling Gaze trigger for Integrity/Humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't it say it's &quot;always a Breaking Point&quot;? I wouldn't impose any additional penalties, just roll at your current Humanity level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:21:28-08:00","id":431619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/431545-unsettling-gaze#post431545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> which seems useful for an older Nosferatu, but not very useful at all for those with low Blood Potency</div> </div> </div> </div>As a small side note, Atrocious helps a lot. Indeed, I think any character who plans to take Unsettling Gaze should probably take Atrocious first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T21:15:45-08:00","id":432222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/431545-unsettling-gaze?p=431619#post431619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a small side note, Atrocious helps a lot. Indeed, I think any character who plans to take Unsettling Gaze should probably take Atrocious first.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T18:47:27-07:00","id":433403,"title":"","content":"My issue with this merit is that most of the time you're going to be using Lashing Out against NPCs, and Humanity is rarely important for NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T18:56:37-07:00","id":433412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/431545-unsettling-gaze?p=433403#post433403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue with this merit is that most of the time you're going to be using Lashing Out against NPCs, and Humanity is rarely important for NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean, theoretically, Conditions aren't important for NPCs, either. Draining their Willpower probably doesn't mean much either. But these things also represent narrative moments that are important. Causing them to experience a breaking point is definitely an unpleasant experience. <br /> <br /> It's definitely more useful against humans than vampires, in my opinion, but considering the amount of mortals you can encounter, that's a pretty good deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:14:36-07:00","id":433501,"title":"","content":"If we are talking purely mechanically:<br /> <br /> vs mortals: You can get them Shaken. Making them easier victims (unless the ST tries to be a dick and never resolves Shaken against you)<br /> <br /> vs Kindred: You can double up on negative Conditions. Bestial from your Lash Out and Competitive or Wanton from the Breaking Point. An opponent who is both Bestial and Competitive is an easy foe to defeat (especially since NPCs rarely have much Willpower to spend).<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Also some fringe benefits, like undoing a Theban Sorcerer, triggering the Clan Bane in a Neonate, pushing an NPC to detach from a Touchstone, etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":".  Added a thought 03-08-2015, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T23:48:14-07:00","id":433633,"title":"","content":"@Saibot: I concede. Those are potentially some very nice benefits.<br /> @Leetspeak: I believe it is -generally- considered bad form for the ST to ignore resolving conditions on NPCs because they can't use Beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T00:18:14-07:00","id":433642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/431545-unsettling-gaze?p=433633#post433633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Saibot: I concede. Those are potentially some very nice benefits.<br /> @Leetspeak: I believe it is -generally- considered bad form for the ST to ignore resolving conditions on NPCs because they can't use Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're misunderstanding my point. I was just talking about the narrative benefit of causing a breaking point is more significant than the mechanical effect of lowering an NPC's essentially non-existent/static Integrity score.<br /> <br /> Or rather, if you feel like there isn't enough mechanical benefit, don't lose sight of that narrative benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}